Commit:     Mark Shank <mark.shank@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Wed Oct 21 15:49:41 2026 -0400

    Narrow more V4.1 decode weights and read them with wider loads
    
    The indexer's q_b weights are FP8 (E4M3) in the original checkpoint, but the GGUF widens them to F16, as it does for the Engram projection. Decode now reads an exact FP8 copy of them, built when the model loads, which halves the bytes read. If any layer can't be converted without loss, every layer keeps reading F16.
    
    The BF16 router and FP8 matvec kernels now load 16 bytes at a time, and the FP8 kernel reads each scale once for both of its rows. They multiply and add in the same order as before, so the results are bit-identical.
    
    The copies are allocated like V4.1's model weights, without Metal hazard tracking. This builds on Ivan Fioravanti's FP8 and BF16 weight copies.
    
    DS4_METAL_DISABLE_V41_INDEXER_E4M3=1 keeps the F16 reads. DS4_METAL_MODEL_TRACKED=1 turns hazard tracking on for the model weights and the copies.

